DURABLE-005 crash-UX record (code-read 2026-10-22)
Owner decision: the program crashes and recovers itself quickly and continues like nothing happened.
Proof boundary: DURABLE-004's kill-the-real-server harness does not exist yet; the reconnect assertions below are proven against the real client with a killed transport.

## reconnect: Reconnection of the tunnel with backoff and without a reload
current: The page holds one WebSocket at /workspace/grpc carrying gRPC frames (internal/transport/cell/tunnel.go). The server ends sockets at an 8h ceiling so the client reconnects and re-authorizes, with 30s ping / 120s idle keepalive; every RPC carries its own Bearer [REDACTED] the tunnel forwards no Authorization or Cookie itself. The wasm client dials with retries disabled because the server owns idempotency. On top of the socket, four backoff schedules disagree: the chat stream retries at 2s doubling to 30s (tools/uxqual/cmd/journeywasm/chat_stream_wasm.go), product invalidation tries 6 times at 500ms-1s then rests 30s (product_invalidation.go, via this package's RunReconnect), agent activity SSE backs off 3s doubling to 60s (persona_chat_service.go), and load-time reads use a 1s/2s/5s/15s retrier (internal/humanwork/chatui/chatux012_retry.go).
gap: No single reconnect policy: four schedules, and the socket-level gRPC reconnect under the wasm dialer is library internals the record could not ground. Nothing proves the page reconnects without a reload after a server restart today.
contract: The tunnel reconnects with backoff and jitter and without a reload; every reconnected RPC re-authorizes from the page credential; consecutive failures draw from a bounded budget (this package exhausts with ErrReconnectExhausted) and a productive round resets the budget. DURABLE-004 proves it against a real kill.

## resubscribe: Resubscription of everything on screen from stored state
current: The chat stream resumes from its stored cursor, with catch-up of gaps through ListPosts, drops a stale cursor and resubscribes immediately, and gives up after 5 fruitless reconnects with the counter reset by a productive round. This package's RunReconnect resumes from the last committed local checkpoint and authoritatively catches the missing range up before the next hint is admitted; the server watches (WatchConversation, journey watch) each end at a 15-minute ceiling. The Agents-page task instead polls every 3s while non-final and skips errors silently, so a restart is a silent stall that resumes with no give-up and no notice. Rollout-in-progress and transcription refresh wiring is ungrounded.
gap: Polling surfaces have no subscription to resume and no notice while stalled; the chat 'working' line is SSE-driven with a locally ticking elapsed clock, matching RED's stuck card when the stream silently dies. Nothing resubscribes a rollout or a transcription view that the record could verify.
contract: A working answer, a running task, a rollout in progress and a transcription each resubscribe from stored state and show their true current state within seconds of recovery; a sequence gap is authoritatively caught up before any hint moves the view.

## gap-ui: What is shown during the gap
current: Reads retry silently by design. The string 'Reconnecting' exists nowhere in the product: only this todo's GREEN text names it. The only terminal state is 'This conversation is no longer updating live.' after about 60s fruitless (2+4+8+16+30s, 5 attempts) with a retry control, localized; the give-up unregisters the stream so the route loader re-reads. Failed actions during an outage DO error: 'We couldn't X. The service did not answer. Try again.'
gap: There is no quiet mid-gap state between silent retry and the 60s terminal notice, and failed actions during a restart surface as errors, against GREEN's 'never an error for a restart'.
contract: Nothing is shown for under two seconds, then a quiet 'Reconnecting...' that never reads as an error; a restart is never an error. Only the spent bounded budget may surface a terminal state, with exactly one retry control.

## drafts-forms: Drafts and half-filled forms kept across the gap and a reload
current: A test-enforced storage boundary lets journeywasm touch only sessionStorage, only for the history hint; localStorage and IndexedDB are forbidden (web031_storage_boundary_native_test.go). Chat drafts are server-persisted instead: a debounced writer stores them in SidebarState.LayoutJson.Drafts via PutSidebar with revision + abort-rebase over 3 attempts, loaded back via GetSidebar, so drafts survive a reload and a server restart; a write failure shows a notice with a manual 'Try again'. Half-filled promotion forms live in in-memory journeyclient state with no persistence found, and are expected lost on reload (search not exhaustive).
gap: Anything not yet pushed to the server draft row, and every promotion form, dies with the page; the storage gate forbids the obvious client-side fix inside journeywasm.
contract: Drafts and half-filled forms are kept across the gap AND across a reload: server-held draft rows where they exist, and a gate exception or server-held session for the rest.

## voice-recording: An unsent voice recording kept across the gap and a reload
current: The recorder holds chunks in memory with a Blob + object-URL preview (tools/uxqual/cmd/journeywasm/chatvoice_recorder_wasm.go). send() runs a 30s timeout; failure lands 'sendfailed' with the bytes kept for a manual retry, cleared only on success or Cancel. A reload loses the recording.
gap: Memory-only bytes plus a storage gate that forbids persisting them: RED's unsent voice recording cannot survive a reload today.
contract: An unsent voice recording is kept across the gap and across a reload, either behind a narrow storage-gate exception or in a server-held resumable upload session keyed like the existing voice-<nanos> identity.

## sessions: Sessions surviving a restart
current: Dev browser login verifies the pasted Bearer [REDACTED] and stores it verbatim in the HttpOnly hcmnext_session cookie for 12h with no server row, so it survives a restart while unexpired and the verifier key is unchanged (internal/humanwork/workspace/handler.go); cookie-for-header substitution needs an explicit flag. OIDC sessions live in Postgres (internal/trust/session/pgstore) and survive restarts, revoked on logout; the in-memory Manager is test-only. After a reload the shell re-issues island Bearer [REDACTED] the cookie, and per-RPC auth re-authenticates the reconnected socket with no re-login while valid.
gap: RED's report that a signed-in session in one browser was gone while another continued is ungrounded: no code path found explains a restart signing exactly one browser out.
contract: Sessions survive a restart; a reconnected page re-authenticates from its credential with no re-login while valid. DURABLE-004 reproduces RED's one-browser-signed-out report or closes it as unreproducible.

## disconnected-actions: An action taken during the gap is queued once or refused plainly
current: Chat send makes one attempt with a 30s timeout; failure restores the text to the draft with a notice, and an identical retry reuses the SAME idempotency key, cleared on success: manual, duplicate-safe, never auto-queued (tools/uxqual/cmd/journeywasm/chat_wasm.go). The only queued case is location share, held while navigator.onLine is false and flushed on 'online'. Sidebar, draft and agent reads offer a manual 'Try again' only. Gap: agent-control and announcement commands mint a fresh randomUUID per click, so a retry after a timeout carries a new key the server cannot dedupe: a possible double-apply.
gap: Nothing auto-queues a disconnected action for replay, and the fresh-key-per-click commands can double-apply on retry-after-timeout.
contract: An action taken during the gap is either queued and sent once on reconnection under one stable idempotency key per user intent, or refused plainly; it is never silently dropped and never sent twice. DURABLE-004 asserts the queued-or-refused property for a mention, a task and an announcement post with a page open during the kill.

